# The project video, as a cue sheet.
#
# Every frame is the real plugin rendering through the real FFGL sequence. This
# is the effect being OPERATED, not a mock-up. Render with:
#
#   ffmpeg -i source.mp4 -f rawvideo -pix_fmt rgba - \
#     | ./build/astest --pipe --size 1920x1080 --fps 30 --script tools/video.cues \
#     | ffmpeg -f rawvideo -pix_fmt rgba -s 1920x1080 -r 30 -i - out.mp4
#
# Syntax: `frame  Parameter Name  value`, ramped between keys.
#
# ⚠️ Mode and Preset are OPTION parameters and must STEP -- two keys one frame
# apart. Ramping Mode sweeps through every selector position on the way, which
# looks like a fault rather than a choice.
#
# 30 fps, so frame = seconds * 30. The order of the piece is the order of the
# README: what it is, then the one idea, then what the idea buys.

# ------------------------------------------------------- 0s: the picture, clean
0    Mix           0.0
0    Mode          0
0    Repeat Rate   0.55
0    Intensity     0.0
0    Head Spread   0.602
0    Input Level   0.5
0    Saturation    0.30
0    Head Wear     0.22
0    Hiss          0.15
0    Dropouts      0.0
0    Wow & Flutter 0.30
0    Wow           0.45
0    Flutter       0.40
0    Scrape        0.20
0    Reverb Time   0.45
0    Dispersion    0.5
0    Echo Volume   0.0
0    Reverb Volume 0.0
0    Direct Volume 1.0
0    Bass          0.5
0    Treble        0.5

# Two seconds of the untouched picture, so there is a before.
60   Mix           0.0
75   Mix           1.0

# --------------------------------------------- 2.5s: one head, and it arrives
# Echo Volume up rather than Mix, so what fades in is the TAPE and not the
# effect -- the direct signal never moves.
75    Echo Volume  0.0
150   Echo Volume  0.85

# ------------------------------------------ 6s: Intensity, so it repeats
180   Intensity    0.0
300   Intensity    0.55

# ------------------------------------- 11s: the Mode Selector, stepping
# Each position held for a second and a half. STEPPED, never ramped.
330   Mode  0
331   Mode  1
375   Mode  1
376   Mode  2
420   Mode  2
421   Mode  3

# ------------------------------- 15.5s: THE ONE IDEA -- Repeat Rate drags
# The signature move, and the reason this is not a frame delay. Slow, so the
# echoes already on the tape can be seen sliding and re-pitching on the way.
465   Repeat Rate  0.55
540   Repeat Rate  0.88
660   Repeat Rate  0.18
780   Repeat Rate  0.55

# --------------------------------- 26s: Intensity toward self-oscillation
780   Intensity    0.55
900   Intensity    0.92
960   Intensity    0.92
1020  Intensity    0.50

# ------------------------------- 34s: Head Spread -- the heads come apart
# Something the hardware could only do with a screwdriver. The tears get large
# and the 1:2:3 rhythm stretches out with them.
1020  Head Spread  0.602
1140  Head Spread  0.90
1200  Head Spread  0.602

# --------------------------------- 40s: the transport comes apart
1200  Wow & Flutter 0.30
1260  Wow & Flutter 0.85
1260  Head Wear     0.22
1320  Head Wear     0.70
1320  Dropouts      0.0
1350  Dropouts      0.45

# ----------------------------- 45s: the tank, and out on all three heads
1350  Mode  3
1351  Mode  10
1350  Reverb Volume 0.0
1410  Reverb Volume 0.75
1380  Wow & Flutter 0.85
1440  Wow & Flutter 0.35
1380  Head Wear     0.70
1440  Head Wear     0.25
1380  Dropouts      0.45
1440  Dropouts      0.0
1440  Intensity     0.50
1530  Intensity     0.62
